{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A prayer of Moses, the man of Elohim</b> — In my opinion: our master Moses composed this prayer, for it is in the plural voice, and the words of David are not so. Furthermore: he begins ה' מעון אתה, and in the Torah מעונה אלהי קדם. Rabbi Moses said: for מעון is from the root of עין מקום מבט עין (a place of looking, the sight of the eye). And what is correct in my eyes: that it is from מעון קדשך, and that is the upper ceiling, as: ויהי בשלם סוכו, and behold, מעונתו parallels סוכו. And the meaning: for the heavens are not truly a dwelling for us; rather You are the true dwelling, and a generation goes and a generation comes, and the dwelling stands, unchanged." "<b>The sense of אתה with the word היית</b> — You alone."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {0 "Resolved 'Rabbi Moses' without bracketed surname; Ibn Ezra frequently cites R. Moses ha-Kohen or R. Moses ibn Gikatilla, but the text gives no further identification."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:45.526941497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}